===== gwi =====
Google Workspace Interface: Gmail from the command line.

Usage: gwi [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  gmail  Gmail: search, read, and label messages via OAuth2
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

===== gwi gmail =====
Gmail: search, read, and label messages via OAuth2

Usage: gwi gmail [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  auth                 Manages Gmail OAuth2 credentials (mirrors the `gmail_auth_status` MCP tool for `status`)
  account              Manages named Gmail accounts (mirrors the `gmail_account_list` MCP tool for `list`)
  search               Searches Gmail messages (mirrors the `gmail_search` MCP tool)
  read                 Reads a single Gmail message (mirrors the `gmail_message_read` MCP tool)
  thread               Reads a Gmail thread (mirrors the `gmail_thread_read` MCP tool)
  label                Manages Gmail labels (mirrors the `gmail_label_list` MCP tool; `add`/`remove` are CLI-only in Phase 1)
  draft                Manages Gmail drafts; never sends or deletes one (mirrors the `gmail_draft_list`/`gmail_draft_show` MCP tools for `list`/`show`; `create`/`update` are CLI-only; #1920)
  sync                 Maintains a durable local archive of a mailbox (CLI-only; no MCP equivalent)
  sync-all             Maintains durable local archives for every account in `.gwi/gmail-sync.yaml`, concurrently (CLI-only; no MCP equivalent; ADR-0068)
  extract-attachments  Retroactively extracts attachments for already-archived messages, without re-fetching from Gmail (CLI-only; no MCP equivalent; purely local, no client/credentials needed; #1510)
  render               Renders one or more archived `.eml` files as human-readable Markdown (CLI-only; no MCP equivalent; purely local, no client/credentials needed; #1513)
  insert               Restores archived `.eml` messages into a mailbox (needs `gmail.modify`; CLI-only; no MCP equivalent; #1655)
  help                 Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see [ADR-0066](../../../docs/adrs/adr-0066.md)). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi gmail auth =====
Manages Gmail OAuth2 credentials (mirrors the `gmail_auth_status` MCP tool for `status`)

Usage: gwi gmail auth [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  import  Imports an OAuth2 client id/secret from a downloaded `client_secret.json`
  login   Runs the Gmail OAuth2 login flow (opens a browser). Interactive-only — login has no MCP equivalent
  logout  Removes the stored Gmail refresh token from settings.json
  status  Shows the current authentication status (mirrors the `gmail_auth_status` MCP tool)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see [ADR-0066](../../../docs/adrs/adr-0066.md)). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi gmail auth import =====
Imports an OAuth2 client id/secret from a downloaded `client_secret.json`

Usage: gwi gmail auth import [OPTIONS] [PATH]

Arguments:
  [PATH]
          Explicit path to client_secret.json. Omit to auto-discover via $GMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET_FILE, ~/.config/gws/client_secret.json, or ~/Downloads/client_secret_*.apps.googleusercontent.com.json

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see [ADR-0066](../../../docs/adrs/adr-0066.md)). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

===== gwi gmail auth login =====
Runs the Gmail OAuth2 login flow (opens a browser). Interactive-only — login has no MCP equivalent

Usage: gwi gmail auth login [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --account <NAME>
          Selects a named Gmail account configured in `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style, mirrors the top-level `--profile`) for this invocation.
          
          Orthogonal to `--profile`: switching the Gmail account never changes which profile is active, and vice versa (see [ADR-0066](../../../docs/adrs/adr-0066.md)). Overrides `GWI_GMAIL_ACCOUNT`. Scoped to the `gmail` subtree — unlike `--profile` it is not usable before the `gmail` subcommand name, only after it (`gmail --account NAME <cmd>` or `gmail <cmd> --account NAME`), so it can't collide with another product's own `--account` flag (Drive has the same one) as more command trees are added.

      --modify
          Request the `gmail.modify` scope in addition to `gmail.readonly`. It is needed by every command that changes the mailbox: `label add`/`remove`, `draft create`/`update` and `insert`. Without this flag, only read access is granted

      --profile <NAME>
          Selects a named credential/config profile from `~/.gwi/settings.json` (AWS-CLI style).
          
          When set, the profile's `env` bundle replaces the base `env` map in the settings-fallback chain (process env still wins); the base map is not consulted. Overrides `GWI_PROFILE`. An unknown name is a hard error listing the known profiles.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

